.externalNativeBuild
.cxx
local.properties
.kotlin

# Release signing — never commit the keystore, its base64, or its passwords.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.jks.base64
keystore.properties

# Google Play service-account key — never commit it (grants release access).
play-credentials.json

# Play store-listing graphics: the icon / feature graphic are large binaries that
# change rarely, so keep those out of git (re-fetch with `bootstrapReleaseListing`
# when you need to touch them). The phone SCREENSHOTS, however, ARE committed —
# they're generated deterministically from the emulator (English UK + Polish) and
# reviewed as diffs, so `publishReleaseListing` pushes them from the repo. The
# listing TEXT (title/short/full descriptions) is committed under app/src/main/play/.
#
# The directory name is dictated by gradle-play-publisher: it publishes exactly
# `/listings/*/graphics/<ImageType.dirName>/*`, and for phone shots that dirName
# is the kebab-case `phone-screenshots` (`phoneScreenshots` is the Play API's
# FIELD name, which GPP never looks for on disk). A dir named anything else is
# silently skipped, so this negation must track ImageType.dirName exactly —
# store-screenshots-test.sh guards that.
app/src/main/play/listings/*/graphics/*
!app/src/main/play/listings/*/graphics/phone-screenshots/
# …but not the capture scratchpad inside it. store-screenshots.sh appends every
# run's shots to candidates/ so nothing is overwritten; you promote the keepers
# up one level by hand. GPP's include pattern is single-segment (`…/*`), so this
# subdir is invisible to the publisher either way — ignoring it just keeps the
# raw pile out of git.
app/src/main/play/listings/*/graphics/phone-screenshots/candidates/
